    {
      "number": 3,
      "section": "A",
      "marks": 5,
      "stem": "Consider the convergent infinite geometric series $4+4\\left(\\dfrac a7\\right)+4\\left(\\dfrac{a^2}{49}\\right)+\\cdots$.",
      "parts": [
        {
          "label": "a",
          "prompt": "State its common ratio $r$.",
          "marks": 1
        },
        {
          "label": "b",
          "prompt": "The sum to infinity is 7. Find $a$.",
          "marks": 4
        }
      ],
      "answerSummary": "$r=a/7$ and $a=3$.",
      "markScheme": [
        {
          "part": "a",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$r=a/7$."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "part": "b",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "M1",
              "text": "Use $S_\\infty=u_1/(1-r)$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$4/(1-a/7)=7$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$4=7-a$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$a=3$, with $|a/7|<1$ as required."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sourcePages": [
        4
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": 4,
      "section": "A",
      "marks": 6,
      "stem": "The graph of $f(x)=p\\cos(qx)+9$, where $q>0$ and $x$ is measured in radians, is shown. It has a local maximum at $A(24,14)$ and a minimum at the $y$-intercept $(0,4)$. The complete cycles visible in the diagram are part of the given information.",
      "parts": [
        {
          "label": "a",
          "prompt": "Find the period of $f$.",
          "marks": 2
        },
        {
          "label": "b",
          "prompt": "State the amplitude.",
          "marks": 1
        },
        {
          "label": "c",
          "prompt": "Find $p$ and $q$.",
          "marks": 3
        }
      ],
      "answerSummary": "$T=16$, amplitude 5, $p=-5$, $q=\\pi/8$.",
      "markScheme": [
        {
          "part": "a",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "M1",
              "text": "From $x=0$ to the marked maximum at 24 there are 1.5 periods."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "The period is 16."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "part": "b",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "The amplitude is $14-9=5$."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "part": "c",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$p=-5$, since $f(0)$ is a minimum."
            },
            {
              "code": "M1",
              "text": "$q=2\\pi/(\\mathrm{period})$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$q=\\pi/8$."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sourcePages": [
        5
      ],
